🔥 WHY HashMap is used in CACHING (this is critical)
What is caching?
Storing data so future access is faster

Example:
DB call = slow
Memory lookup = fast

🧠 Why HashMap is PERFECT for caching
Caching needs:
Fast lookup
Key → Value
In-memory
Replaceable values

HashMap gives:
O(1) lookup
Key → Value
Memory-based
Replace on duplicate key

🧪 Real example (simple)
Map<Integer, User> cache = new HashMap<>();
User getUser(int id) {
    if (cache.containsKey(id)) {
        return cache.get(id);   // FAST
    }
    User user = dbCall(id);     // SLOW
    cache.put(id, user);
    return user;
}

🧠 This is why interviewers ALWAYS say:
“HashMap is used for caching”

🔥 Why LinkedHashMap for LRU Cache
HashMap alone doesn’t know:
which entry is oldest
LinkedHashMap:
remembers access order
So:
LinkedHashMap → eviction logic

That’s why:
HashMap → cache
LinkedHashMap → LRU cache

